Source: #2444 Friction. Supersedes the uncontrolled #2444 entry at roster ebf81fc1d. The repository-local `.git/info/exclude` carries a bare `seat/` line, so `git add -A` silently leaves a new file under tools/audit/seat/ untracked. #2444's two new instruments needed `git add -f`, and a seat that misses this hands off code with no instrument. The exclude is local configuration and not part of the tree, so it was reported and not changed; the group decides where to put the guidance (a brief step or a seat-start check).
Control (precondition): in the affected clone, `touch tools/audit/seat/zz_probe.py; git check-ignore -v tools/audit/seat/zz_probe.py` prints `.git/info/exclude:<n>:seat/	tools/audit/seat/zz_probe.py` and `git status --short` does not list the file (the line number <n> varies by clone). Null control: in a fresh clone without that line, the same `git check-ignore -v` prints nothing (rc=1) and `git status --short` lists the file as `??`. Remove the probe file afterwards.
Re-measure: before the brief states how many seats are affected, run the check in each seat's checkout and worktree (`git rev-parse --git-common-dir` for the shared exclude) and count the ones that print the exclude line.
